From: Package maintainers <packages@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] read system policy from administrator, runtime, and vendor paths
Source: downstream
Upstream: not submitted; suitable for upstream review

Read persistent administrator policy below /etc before temporary machine
policy below /run and package defaults below /usr. Merge drop-in directories
by filename, with the higher-priority copy shadowing the lower-priority copy.
Keep explicit module arguments authoritative.

Cover the two readers that the first pass missed. pam_namespace_helper read
only the administrator namespace.conf, so a vendor or transient file that
pam_namespace itself honored was invisible to the helper that prepares the
polyinstantiated directories. pam_securetty walked the administrator file and
then the vendor file with no transient tier at all. Both now follow the same
administrator, runtime, vendor order as the rest of the package.

